In LangGraph, edges define how execution moves from one node (agent/function) to another. Think of nodes as tasks and edges as the roads connecting those tasks.

. Edge (Normal Edge)

A normal edge always moves from one node to the next.

Flow
START
  |
  v
Node A
  |
  v
Node B
  |
  v
END

No decision is made.

Example
graph.add_edge("planner", "researcher")
graph.add_edge("researcher", "writer")
graph.add_edge("writer", END)
Execution
Planner
   ↓
Researcher
   ↓
Writer
   ↓
END

